9	 * (2026-09-11).  The load side (3 ldr per element: top dead scratch load +
10	 * 2-src srcA/srcB) and the rotating ALU (add/eor/and/orr by i%4) are kept
11	 * IDENTICAL to the rowmajor parent; the only change is a THIRD store per
12	 * element: an extra dead str of the ALU result to an independent junk
13	 * buffer (junk is never read back).  Together with str4 this builds a
14	 * store-count gradient: 2 (parent) / 3 / 4 str per element at constant
15	 * 3 ldr + rot ALU.
16	 *   If trigger rate survives across 2->3->4  -> store count is a free
17	 *      dimension (AGU/LSU store-side pressure does not gate the fault)
18	 *   If it collapses at 3 (or between 3 and 4) -> the 2-str back-to-back
19	 *      adjacency / timing budget is part of the trigger recipe
20	 * Note the known risk: any instruction-count change perturbs scheduling
21	 * (see the unaligned/nop precedents); a 0-fail here is therefore
22	 * ambiguous between "store pressure kills it" and "layout shift kills
23	 * it" -- str4 vs str3 shares the layout-shift confound, so the gradient
24	 * SHAPE (monotone collapse vs cliff) is the informative signal.
25	 * @endparblock
