16	 * cell:
17	 *   slot_mask 0b111  -> res itself wrong: upstream load/ALU error
18	 *   slot_mask 1<<k   -> store k's own write path corrupted the value
19	 *   rates s0 vs s1 vs s2 -> position-dependent store-path failure rates
20	 *
21	 * Hot loop is IDENTICAL to str3 (3 ldr: top dead scratch + 2-src
22	 * srcA/srcB; rotating ALU add/eor/and/orr by i%4; 3 str of the same res
23	 * to temp/junk/dst in that order; same TEST_LOOP count 1<<13).  The
24	 * per-sweep section replaces the parent's single memcmp(dst,...) with
25	 * THREE memcmps -- temp, junk and dst each vs the golden -- all run
26	 * unconditionally (never gated on dst), so junk-only and temp-only
27	 * errors are caught.  On any mismatch a noinline cold scan records, per
28	 * mismatching index, WHICH store slot(s) are wrong plus all three slot
29	 * actuals and a cold re-read of srcA/srcB (load- vs ALU-error
30	 * classification, as in rowmajor_dump).
31	 *
32	 * Within-run slot-rate comparison (s0 vs s1 vs s2) is immune to the
33	 * check-section layout confound: all three slots share the same loop,
34	 * the same sweep and the same timing.  Cross-test rate comparison
35	 * (str3_checkall vs str3) is NOT valid -- the per-sweep section grew
36	 * from 1 to 3 memcmps (same known confound as str4_checkall); this test
37	 * is a slot classifier, not a rate point.
38	 *
39	 * Records go to /var/tmp/neon_rot_ldr_at_top_str3_checkall_<pid>.bin
40	 * (on-disk, per the 09-08 panic lesson: /tmp is tmpfs and loses records
41	 * on crash).
42	 * @endparblock
43	 */
44	
45	#include "sandstone.h"
46	#include <cstdint>
47	#include <cstring>
48	#include <fcntl.h>
49	#include <unistd.h>
