13	 * the SAME element index, i.e. two addresses 16 KiB apart (same offset
14	 * within each buffer) — far apart in different cache lines AND different
15	 * sets, which is what makes "splice" distinguishable from "misaligned
16	 * window": neighbouring dual sources produce identical bytes for both
17	 * failure modes, far-apart sources expose cross-line byte mixing.
18	 *
19	 * This variant keeps the hot loop byte-identical to the GPS chassis and
20	 * changes ONLY the fill: srcB is filled at a NEAR address instead —
21	 * srcB[i] element carries the tag of buffer offset (i * 16 + 8), i.e.
22	 * the word IMMEDIATELY AFTER srcA[i]'s lane 1 word in address space is
23	 * simulated as "the other source".  WRONG — see corrected design below.
24	 *
25	 * CORRECTED DESIGN (after first-signature review, 09-13 evening): the
26	 * first GPS round showed the dominant signature is same-buffer FIELD
27	 * SUBSTITUTION from a NEIGHBOURING srcA word (156/156 sources in srcA,
28	 * distance ±8..±28 elements).  The K5 question for THIS signature is
29	 * therefore: does the substitution source follow the ADDRESS (near
30	 * neighbour of the failing load's address, whichever buffer it belongs
31	 * to) or the BUFFER IDENTITY / port (stays srcA-only even when the
32	 * address neighbour is srcB)?  To answer it, this variant INTERLEAVES
33	 * the two sources in one address space:
34	 *
35	 *   single buffer src[2*i]   = "A-family" word pair (magic 0xA5A5)
36	 *   single buffer src[2*i+1] = "B-family" word pair (magic 0x5A5A)
37	 *
38	 * The hot loop loads A from src[2*i] and B from src[2*i+1] — adjacent
39	 * addresses (32 B apart), alternating family magic every element.  The
40	 * address-neighbour of every load is ALWAYS the other family.  Outcomes:
41	 *   - substitution source still "A-only"  -> source follows buffer/
42	 *     port identity, address proximity is not the driver;
43	 *   - substitution source becomes "the address neighbour" (i.e. for a
44	 *     failing element i, the substituted fields come from src[2*i±1],
45	 *     the OTHER family) -> proximity-driven cross-talk (E6-family);
46	 *   - true A+B splice words appear (already detectable) -> steering.
47	 *
48	 * Engineering: hot loop loads via the same asm ldr q, same i%4 rotating
49	 * ALU, same back-to-back str/str, same rowmajor alternating sweeps, same
50	 * cold-path memcmp + five-buffer dump discipline as the GPS chassis.
51	 * The only deltas vs GPS chassis: one interleaved source buffer instead
52	 * of two parallel ones (same total footprint, same load count), and the
53	 * dump layout records the interleaved buffer twice (slots srcA/srcB
54	 * hold the same pointer's first/second half view for classifier
55	 * compatibility).  No LCG seed fixing; auto-seed only.
56	 * @endparblock
57	 */
