1	/**
2	 * @copyright
3	 * Copyright 2022 Intel Corporation.
4	 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
5	 *
6	 * @test @b neon_rot_ldr_at_top_rowmajor_k3res
7	 * @parblock
8	 * K3 residency cell: 4x-L1D footprint (2026-09-13,
9	 * docs/CORE179_READPATH_LOCALIZATION_CAMPAIGN_20260913.md §5 K3 axis).
10	 *
11	 * Adjudicates whether the substitution/misaligned-window SOURCE lines
12	 * are L1D-resident at failure time.  The champion footprint (16 KiB
13	 * per buffer, 4 buffers = 64 KiB total) sits inside the 64 KiB L1D of
14	 * Kunpeng 920, so in the GPS chassis every source word the classifier
15	 * ever identifies was necessarily L1D-resident.  This cell scales the
16	 * working set 4x (4096 elements per buffer = 64 KiB per buffer, 256
17	 * KiB total) so a random sweep evicts most lines before they are
18	 * re-referenced: if the field-substitution sources REMAIN at
19	 * near-neighbour distances (+-1..3 lines) they are still resident
20	 * (recently touched by the sweep itself) and the cell distinguishes
21	 * nothing; but if the signature SURVIVES the footprint change at the
22	 * same rate while the far-neighbour (evicted) sources DISAPPEAR from
23	 * the histogram, residency is a necessary condition for the source —
24	 * pointing INSIDE the L1D array / way-select level rather than any
25	 * later pipeline stage.
26	 *
27	 * Pre-registered readouts:
28	 *   - rate collapses -> the 64 KiB-resident champion footprint is part
29	 *     of the trigger recipe (footprint sensitivity, feeds the
30	 *     footprint-independent-of-L1D-size memory re-check);
31	 *   - rate holds + source-distance histogram still tight (all resident
32	 *     neighbours) -> no eviction exposure, cell is uninformative for
33	 *     residency but the rate-invariance under 4x footprint is still a
34	 *     useful negative;
35	 *   - rate holds + histogram grows FAR sources -> far (evicted)
36	 *     sources participate; L1D-internal selection is disfavoured.
37	 *
38	 * Dump: same five-buffer discipline (buffers are 4x larger; dump files
39	 * ~320 KiB each).  GPS tags unchanged — byte_off still fits 16b
40	 * (max 65535 >= 65536-16).  CAREFUL: byte offsets reach 65520, which
41	 * still fits the 16b field; the classifier's byte_off decode is
